  "query_preview": "../Sunday through Wednesday/... \nConfidence is growing in a set up to bring warmer temperatures to\nthe southern panhandle, Hyder in particular, through the \nbeginning of next week. Sunday is expected to be dry with clearing\nskies through the day across the entire area before rain chances \nincrease again from Yakutat northward on Monday. The rest of the \npanhandle is anticipated to remain dry with sunnier skies, which \nwill be the deciding factor in how warm temperatures will get. \nCloudier skies then look to move into the northern panhandle on \nTuesday, which will cause temperature to remain slightly cooler \nthan Monday's. However, Wednesday is anticipated to be the warmest\nday next week in the central and southern panhandle given that \nskies remain clear to allow for optimal daytime heating.",
